    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0090" n="8" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg8"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commanding General, United States Military Mission
                        in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Deane</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Joint Chiefs of Staff </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Excerpt]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d10-f1"/>
                    </seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">eyes only</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-17">17 October
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">M 21412.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>. . . Stalin then said that Mr. Hopkins, with the approval of the President, had
                    talked with Mr. Gromyko and he had indicated that the President was anxious to
                    meet with Marshal Stalin somewhere in the Black Sea area. He said unequivocally
                    that he would be <pb facs="0091" n="9" xml:id="pg9"/> delighted to meet the
                    President and was prepared to so do toward the end of November. . . .</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
